WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.617
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online B one, Book one.

2
00:00:05.917 --> 00:00:08.944
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.244 --> 00:00:15.031
Unit one: Introducing Myself. Today you will introduce yourself and describe your personality.

4
00:00:15.331 --> 00:00:18.053
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:22.384
Part one: words. You will learn twelve new words.

6
00:00:23.250 --> 00:00:24.054
Name.

7
00:00:25.050 --> 00:00:27.154
Name means the word people call you.

8
00:00:27.750 --> 00:00:29.332
My name is Sophea.

9
00:00:29.917 --> 00:00:32.128
Your turn. Say: Name.

10
00:00:34.967 --> 00:00:35.747
Name.

11
00:00:36.483 --> 00:00:37.368
Age.

12
00:00:38.383 --> 00:00:40.557
Age means how many years old you are.

13
00:00:41.150 --> 00:00:43.417
At my age, I'm in Grade 7.

14
00:00:44.017 --> 00:00:46.448
Your turn. Say: Age.

15
00:00:49.300 --> 00:00:50.197
Age.

16
00:00:50.950 --> 00:00:52.160
Nationality.

17
00:00:53.150 --> 00:00:55.881
Nationality means the country you belong to.

18
00:00:56.483 --> 00:00:58.703
My nationality is Cambodian.

19
00:00:59.317 --> 00:01:02.143
Your turn. Say: Nationality.

20
00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:06.233
Nationality.

21
00:01:06.983 --> 00:01:08.101
Introduce.

22
00:01:09.117 --> 00:01:11.441
Introduce means to tell people who you are.

23
00:01:12.050 --> 00:01:13.678
Let me introduce myself.

24
00:01:14.283 --> 00:01:16.982
Your turn. Say: Introduce.

25
00:01:19.833 --> 00:01:20.881
Introduce.

26
00:01:21.617 --> 00:01:22.560
Classmate.

27
00:01:23.550 --> 00:01:26.409
Classmate means a student in the same class as you.

28
00:01:27.017 --> 00:01:29.074
My new classmate sits next to me.

29
00:01:29.683 --> 00:01:32.672
Your turn. Say: Classmate.

30
00:01:35.533 --> 00:01:36.534
Classmate.

31
00:01:37.283 --> 00:01:38.226
Hobby.

32
00:01:39.217 --> 00:01:42.493
Hobby means something you enjoy doing in your free time.

33
00:01:43.083 --> 00:01:44.375
My hobby is drawing.

34
00:01:44.983 --> 00:01:47.334
Your turn. Say: Hobby.

35
00:01:50.200 --> 00:01:50.934
Hobby.

36
00:01:51.683 --> 00:01:52.568
Favorite.

37
00:01:53.583 --> 00:01:56.024
Favorite means liked more than all the others.

38
00:01:56.617 --> 00:01:58.477
Blue is my favorite color.

39
00:01:59.083 --> 00:02:01.782
Your turn. Say: Favorite.

40
00:02:04.633 --> 00:02:05.483
Favorite.

41
00:02:06.250 --> 00:02:07.077
Friendly.

42
00:02:08.083 --> 00:02:10.733
Friendly means kind and pleasant to other people.

43
00:02:11.317 --> 00:02:13.258
Everyone in my class is friendly.

44
00:02:13.850 --> 00:02:16.282
Your turn. Say: Friendly.

45
00:02:19.133 --> 00:02:20.134
Friendly.

46
00:02:20.883 --> 00:02:21.629
Shy.

47
00:02:22.617 --> 00:02:25.406
Shy means nervous about talking to new people.

48
00:02:26.017 --> 00:02:27.703
I was shy on my first day.

49
00:02:28.317 --> 00:02:30.574
Your turn. Say: Shy.

50
00:02:33.433 --> 00:02:34.527
Shy.

51
00:02:35.283 --> 00:02:36.261
Outgoing.

52
00:02:37.250 --> 00:02:40.306
Outgoing means happy to meet and talk to new people.

53
00:02:40.917 --> 00:02:42.870
My sister is very outgoing.

54
00:02:43.483 --> 00:02:46.101
Your turn. Say: Outgoing.

55
00:02:48.967 --> 00:02:50.235
Outgoing.

56
00:02:50.983 --> 00:02:51.683
Greet.

57
00:02:52.683 --> 00:02:54.799
Greet means to say hello to someone.

58
00:02:55.383 --> 00:02:57.232
We greet our teacher every morning.

59
00:02:57.817 --> 00:02:59.935
Your turn. Say: Greet.

60
00:03:02.800 --> 00:03:03.406
Greet.

61
00:03:04.150 --> 00:03:05.499
Nice to meet you.

62
00:03:06.483 --> 00:03:10.201
Nice to meet you means a polite thing to say when you meet someone new.

63
00:03:10.817 --> 00:03:13.283
Hi, I'm Dara. Nice to meet you!

64
00:03:13.883 --> 00:03:16.896
Your turn. Say: Nice to meet you.

65
00:03:19.733 --> 00:03:21.303
Nice to meet you.

66
00:03:22.100 --> 00:03:25.925
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

67
00:03:26.783 --> 00:03:29.763
Hello! I'm Ms. Emma. What's your name?

68
00:03:30.850 --> 00:03:33.618
Hi, I'm Visal. Nice to meet you!

69
00:03:34.717 --> 00:03:37.520
Nice to meet you too. How old are you?

70
00:03:38.617 --> 00:03:41.986
I'm thirteen years old, and I'm Cambodian.

71
00:03:43.083 --> 00:03:44.967
Are you shy or outgoing?

72
00:03:46.083 --> 00:03:50.187
I'm a little shy at first, but I'm friendly. My hobby is football.

73
00:03:51.333 --> 00:03:52.660
Part three: grammar.

74
00:03:53.517 --> 00:03:57.757
Grammar focus: Simple present: be plus adjective.

75
00:03:58.057 --> 00:03:59.186
Look at the pattern.

76
00:03:59.883 --> 00:04:01.070
I am friendly.

77
00:04:01.983 --> 00:04:03.182
She is shy.

78
00:04:04.083 --> 00:04:05.410
We are outgoing.

79
00:04:06.367 --> 00:04:09.783
Use am with I, is with he/she/it, and are with you/we/they.

80
00:04:10.517 --> 00:04:13.262
Be careful! Don't say: She are shy.

81
00:04:15.200 --> 00:04:16.712
Say: She is shy.

82
00:04:17.012 --> 00:04:18.849
Use 'is' with he, she and it.

83
00:04:19.633 --> 00:04:22.588
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

84
00:04:23.400 --> 00:04:24.575
Meet Sophea.

85
00:04:24.875 --> 00:04:28.094
Hi, my name is Sophea, and I am thirteen years old.

86
00:04:29.100 --> 00:04:32.655
My nationality is Cambodian, and I live in Phnom Penh.

87
00:04:33.667 --> 00:04:37.245
I am friendly and outgoing, so I like meeting new classmates.

88
00:04:38.233 --> 00:04:41.138
My favorite hobby is drawing animals.

89
00:04:42.133 --> 00:04:46.086
When I meet someone new, I smile and say, 'Nice to meet you!'

90
00:04:47.200 --> 00:04:51.387
Part five: quiz. Three questions. Are you ready?

91
00:04:52.250 --> 00:04:53.530
She blank shy.

92
00:04:53.830 --> 00:04:56.717
A, is. B, am. C, are.

93
00:05:00.267 --> 00:05:02.115
The answer is A: is.

94
00:05:03.250 --> 00:05:05.842
Happy to meet and talk to new people is blank.

95
00:05:06.142 --> 00:05:09.563
A, outgoing. B, shy. C, favorite.

96
00:05:13.100 --> 00:05:15.227
The answer is A: outgoing.

97
00:05:16.383 --> 00:05:18.360
The country you belong to is your blank.

98
00:05:18.660 --> 00:05:22.162
A, nationality. B, hobby. C, age.

99
00:05:25.700 --> 00:05:27.874
The answer is A: nationality.

100
00:05:29.067 --> 00:05:32.265
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

101
00:05:33.117 --> 00:05:35.790
How would you introduce yourself to a new classmate?

102
00:05:44.583 --> 00:05:46.478
Now listen to Visal.

103
00:05:46.778 --> 00:05:56.030
I would say, 'Hi, I'm Dara. Nice to meet you!' I am thirteen. I am friendly, and my hobby is playing football.

104
00:05:56.330 --> 00:05:57.912
Excellent answer, Visal!

105
00:05:58.817 --> 00:06:04.395
Great work! Now you can use twelve new words and simple present: be plus adjective.

106
00:06:04.695 --> 00:06:09.228
Today's value is friendliness. Smile and say hello to everyone.

107
00:06:09.528 --> 00:06:11.890
See you in Unit two. Goodbye!

108
00:06:12.190 --> 00:06:15.144
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

